  This section will demonstrate that a discrete signal needs to be sampled at at least twice the highest
  frequency of its spectrum.
  This minimal sampling frequency / rate is called the Nyquist rate.

  Or, addressing the problem from the other end, for a given sampling rate, the maximal frequency achievable
  is half the sampling frequency, and it's called the Nyquist frequency.



